<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">29 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 29 December, from 1170 to 1940.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/canterbury" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/canterbury.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1170">1170 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">856 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Thomas Becket is murdered in Canterbury Cathedral</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Four knights, believing they were carrying out Henry II's wishes, killed Archbishop Thomas Becket in his cathedral. Becket was canonised in 1173, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canterbury">Canterbury</a> became one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s great pilgrimage sites.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1503">1503 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">523 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gonzalo Fernández de Córdoba routs the French on the Garigliano</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After weeks of stalemate on the river <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garigliano">Garigliano</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gonzalo-fernandez-de-cordoba">Gonzalo Fernández de Córdoba</a>'s Spanish army crossed by surprise and routed the French under Ludovico II of Saluzzo. After the French surrender at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaeta">Gaeta</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> controlled the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-garigliano-1503">Battle of the Garigliano</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gonzalo-fernandez-de-cordoba">Gonzalo Fernández de Córdoba</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludovico-ii-marquis-of-saluzzo">Ludovico II of Saluzzo</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1778">1778 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">248 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British forces capture Savannah</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A British expedition took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savannah">Savannah</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, opening a new campaign in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-south">American South</a>. The southern strategy brought early gains but ended with surrender at Yorktown in 1781.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-south">American South</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savannah">Savannah</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1812">1812 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">214 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">USS Constitution defeats and captures HMS Java off Brazil</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a three-hour single-ship action off the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, the American frigate USS Constitution defeated and captured HMS <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, a former French frigate taken by the British in 1811. Java had 426 aboard, the Constitution 475.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-1812">War of 1812</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1835">1835 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">191 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Treaty of New Echota cedes Cherokee lands east of the Mississippi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">US commissioners and a small minority faction of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cherokee">Cherokee</a> signed a treaty at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-echota">New Echota</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, ceding all Cherokee lands east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a>. Rejected by Principal Chief John Ross and most Cherokee, it led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trail-of-tears">Trail of Tears</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-new-echota">Treaty of New Echota</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cherokee">Cherokee</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1845">1845 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">181 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Texas becomes the 28th US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Nine years after winning independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> was admitted to the Union as a slave state. The annexation helped provoke the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexican-american-war">Mexican-American War</a> the following year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1890">1890 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">136 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US troops massacre Lakota at Wounded Knee</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">While disarming a band of Lakota at Wounded Knee <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a>, South Dakota, the 7th Cavalry opened fire, killing some 250 to 300 men, women and children. It marked the end of the Plains wars.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Firebombs start the 'Second Great Fire of London'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">German bombers dropped thousands of incendiaries on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">City of London</a>, starting some 1,500 fires. Much of the square mile burned, but St Paul's Cathedral survived amid the smoke.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li></ol>
